{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d7e5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a94e-f9b9-7860-b0c6-fdeb793e4d2e"},"sequence":2637,"recorded_at":1780531400005269,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bdb55aec-3668-4dc2-8767-4018e566a62d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bdb55aec-3668-4dc2-8767-4018e566a62d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bdb55aec-3668-4dc2-8767-4018e566a62d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a95f-ae2f-7a43-9ebc-4ce1461eafba"},"task_id":"01a0a95f-ae2f-7a43-9ebc-4ce1461eafba","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a95f-ae2f-7a43-9ebc-4ce1461eafba","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n1|# Runner Control\n2|\n3|Native macOS menu-bar app for installed GitHub Actions runners on the current Mac.\n4|\n5|- Click the lightning icon in the menu bar for individual or combined start/stop controls.\n6|- Stopping CI requires confirmation because it can interrupt a build.\n7|- Opening or quitting the app does not start or stop CI automatically. Quitting with an active service shows a reminder.\n8|- Double-clicking the application again also opens a control window.\n9|- Opening the app preserves each service’s existing login startup policy. Existing `.command` controls remain compatible.\n10|- Displayed state comes from local launchd, not GitHub's delayed online/busy status.\n11|- Each enabled runner can execute a job; multiple registrations may run concurrently.\n12|- Missing registrations, invalid service manifests, command failures and paths with spaces are rejected and surfaced.\n13|\n14|## Identity\n15|\n16|Bundle ID: `works.relux.runnercontrol`  \n17|Development team: `262RZ595FP` (Relux Works)  \n18|Platform: macOS 14+, universal Apple Silicon + Intel build supplied.  \n19|Local builds use Apple Development. Public releases require Developer ID Application and Apple notarization.\n20|\n21|## Build\n22|\n23|Requires Xcode, Tuist and the configured development team in Xcode.\n24|\n25|```sh\n26|./Scripts/build.sh\n27|```\n28|\n29|The result is `.temp/products/RunnerControl.app`. If changing the scaffold configuration, run `ios-app-manager generate macos-app --config ios-app-manager.json` before building. Native generator source: https://github.com/relux-works/skill-ios-app-manager.\n30|\n31|## Tests\n32|\n33|```sh\n34|swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore\n35|RUN_LAUNCH_AGENT_INTEGRATION=1 swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore\n36|```\n37|\n38|The integration option starts and stops only a unique temporary sleep service, never a production GitHub runner. Tests cover reducers, flow errors, idempotency, missing/permission states, path validation, output handling and real launchd lifecycle. No UI tests are included.\n39|\n40|For logs and JUnit output use `Scripts/run-macos-package-tests.sh` from https://github.com/relux-works/skill-ios-testing-tools with `--package Packages/RunnerControlCore --output .temp/macos-tests`.\n41|\n42|## Architecture\n43|\n44|The app owns a single Relux runtime in `AppRegistry`; reopening a popover cannot recreate it. UI containers map state to plain page props/reactions. Core owns a HybridState, reducer, actor flow and actor launchd adapter. Process output is file-backed to avoid pipe deadlocks, commands have a timeout, and subprocess arguments are passed without a shell.\n45|\n46|At launch, the app discovers `manual-service.plist` files in immediate subdirectories of `~/Library/GitHubActions` and standard `actions.runner.*.plist` files in `~/Library/LaunchAgents`. It reads the registration name and GitHub scope from `.runner`, uses the actual service label/path, and deduplicates registrations. Discovery does not execute scripts, alter services or register runners. Arbitrary folder selection and GitHub sign-in are planned, not implemented. The app does not store a GitHub token or modify repository workflows.\n47|\n48|## Releases and automatic updates\n49|\n50|The app uses Sparkle 2.10.0. Its menu offers manual update checks and separate automatic checking/download settings. Updating the app does not stop independently running CI services.\n51|\n52|After the first successful release, the latest DMG is available at:\n53|https://github.com/relux-works/runner-control/releases/latest/download/RunnerControl.dmg\n54|\n55|The signed update archive is announced at:\n56|https://github.com/relux-works/runner-control/releases/latest/download/appcast.xml\n57|\n58|See [RELEASING.md](RELEASING.md) for host setup and release steps. Apple signing and notarization credentials are configured on macbook-iv. Download links become available after the first successful release workflow.","final_result":true}}}
