dit selected repository access for an app-managed org runner from the app. A generic GitHub-settings link alone does not satisfy the user goal. Reuse accepted group ownership, server/scope/agentID verification and current API membership; preserve protections for imported shared/unowned groups (explicit takeover/scope handling, no silent group-wide edits). Personal-account runners remain per-repository registrations with clear add/remove flow. Document actual UI entry point and production-entry tests. This is integration of already approved access management, not new scope.\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 1341,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 336,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
