{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000f181","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a94e-f9b9-7860-b0c6-fdeb793e4d2e"},"sequence":5915,"recorded_at":1780531400011825,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bdb55aec-3668-4dc2-8767-4018e566a62d","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"bdb55aec-3668-4dc2-8767-4018e566a62d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bdb55aec-3668-4dc2-8767-4018e566a62d"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Catalog lifecycle work is handed off to review (`to-review`, checklist 15/15).\n\nWhat shipped: versioned persistent catalog with canonical dedupe, manual/standard discovery plus unsupported read-only kinds, user-folder import with no-space relocation, separate local/remote/operation states with truthful busy/stale/offline UI, individual and bulk power with confirmed stop, manifest/`_diag` log access with redaction, effective login-start model (external `RunAtLoad=true` correctly shows OFF; the toggle really registers/unregisters login without touching live services or foreign plists), typed stopped-only unregister on the shared installer lease versus entry-only removal, fresh API group membership with an in-app repository editor (owned apply, shared takeover, stale refusal), full menu + management-window UI, universal README onboarding, and a signed 1.2.0 candidate in `.temp/products`.\n\nEvidence: AC coverage 18 of 19 rows driven through production entry points (row 18 is the stated manual-UI bound, no UI tests per task); 197 core tests green plus launchd integration green; 17 narrowing mutants all killed with zero survivors, including one that preserves the searched token and runs the behavioral suite; native build succeeded with `codesign --verify` clean. Both production runners stayed `running` with one process each throughout, and the production fixture was never mutated. Outcome artifact `TASK-260916-304bw2_catalog-lifecycle-outcome.md` is attached; the candidate is left uncommitted in the Story worktree for snapshot.","reason":null}}
